.TH GRZ-CONSOLE 1 "2026-09-03" "Green-Roomz 0.1.0" "Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
grz-console, console.sh \- local Green-Roomz operator board
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./console.sh
.P
.B CONSOLE_ONCE=1
.B ./console.sh
.P
.B USAGE_FILE=
.I path
.B HEALTH_URL=
.I url
.B ./console.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B console.sh
is the local operator board shipped with the portable pack (invoked as
.B grz-console
in this manual). It prints to stdout / a file only. It never scrapes PIDs into
an HTTP endpoint and never invents occupancy.
.P
Default mode prints the board every 2 seconds until Ctrl-C.
.B CONSOLE_ONCE=1
prints once and exits. Portable
.B start.sh
may also write a one-shot board to
.IR data/console.txt .
.P
The board is how the operator sees running processes
.B and
combined L0–L3 fill. Prefer it over an internal narration from a cognitive agent.
.SH BOARD
Each pass prints:
.IP \(bu 2
Product line (Green-Roomz console) and host / time (America/Los_Angeles and UTC)
.IP \(bu 2
.B GRZ_ROOT
.IP \(bu 2
.B node :8080
listen pid, threads, RSS, CPU percent — or
.I pid=none (not listening)
.IP \(bu 2
.B llama :8187
same
.IP \(bu 2
GGUF files under
.I models/
with on-disk size (file size is not occupancy)
.IP \(bu 2
.B GET
.I $HEALTH_URL
(default
.BR http://127.0.0.1:8080/health )
truncated status / policy / ready aliases
.IP \(bu 2
Occupancy from
.I $USAGE_FILE
only (default
.IR $GRZ_ROOT/data/operator-usage.json )
.SH OCCUPANCY
.B 70% fill is L0+L1+L2+L3 COMBINED,
not L0 alone. L3 is will / identity last-level on-mind cache. See
.IR docs/strong-mind-will.md
and
.IR docs/diagrams/memory-stack.md .
.P
The console never computes a fill percent. It only echoes measured fields from
the drop-in JSON:
.TP
.B source
Who measured it (use
.B operator
for a manual drop).
.TP
.B prompt_tokens , completion_tokens , total_tokens
Integers from the run. Omit a field rather than guess.
.TP
.B context_fill_pct
Total cache fill L0+L1+L2+L3 combined (percent). Use JSON
.B null
if unmeasured. Printed as
.B total cache fill L0-L3=<n>%
plus a reminder that the 70% hold is combined.
.P
If the file is absent:
.IP
usage: unknown (drop data/operator-usage.json — do not guess)
.P
If the file is present but not valid JSON, or has no token/fill fields, the
board says so and still does not guess.
.P
Copy
.I data/operator-usage.example.json
to
.I data/operator-usage.json
and fill
.B real
numbers. Do not pack a fake filled file. Install refresh must not overwrite
.IR data/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GRZ_ROOT
Pack root. Defaults to the directory containing
.BR console.sh .
.TP
.B USAGE_FILE
Path to the occupancy JSON. Default
.IR $GRZ_ROOT/data/operator-usage.json .
.TP
.B HEALTH_URL
Health endpoint. Default
.BR http://127.0.0.1:8080/health .
.TP
.B CONSOLE_ONCE
If
.BR 1 ,
print once and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I console.sh
This board (portable pack root).
.TP
.I data/operator-usage.json
Operator
.B /usage
drop-in.
.TP
.I data/operator-usage.example.json
Schema only.
.TP
.I data/console.txt
Optional one-shot capture from
.BR start.sh .
.TP
.I data/serve.log
Gateway TTY tee (not this board).
.SH NOTES
Pid discovery uses
.BR ss (8)
then
.BR lsof (8)
then
.BR fuser (1)
on the listen port. RSS/threads come from
.I /proc/<pid>/status
when present (Linux). On Windows/Android the pack may not ship this script;
use the serve TTY and
.I help\\index.html
instead.
.P
Do not stop live listeners on :8080/:8187 from a docs-only session. Do not
point this board at a foreign host. Do not use Windows
.B stop.cmd
against a Linux cursor serve.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR green-roomz (1),
.IR docs/strong-mind-will.md ,
.IR docs/diagrams/serve-topology.md ,
.IR docs/diagrams/memory-stack.md
